    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d635">

                <pb facs="0993" n="967" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg967"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/5–2854: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the United States Delegation</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d635-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-28T16:18:00-04:00">May 28, 1954—4:18
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tedul 137. Eyes only for the Under Secretary
                    from the Secretary. It seems to me that there is a growing possibility that the
                    DVR cease fire proposal might develop into form of <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        facto</hi> partition which Eden might
                    be expected to encourage and which French might find impossible to refuse but
                    which Associated States would oppose.</p>
                <p>If this situation should arise we would face necessity for very difficult
                    decision and I hope it would be possible for you to inform me before taking
                    irrevocable position so that I could consult with the President. This would of
                    course have bearing on paragraph 5 of your President-approved instructions
                        (Tosec 138).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d635-f2"
                    /></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
